# Story 1: What Is Rysh? (60s)
# Hook: A terminal that thinks. Shell mode runs commands. Prompt mode talks to AI.
# Duration: 60s
# Source: story-001-what-is-rysh.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 8

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
A terminal that thinks. Shell mode runs commands, prompt mode talks to AI -- and every pane is both.

[00:04.0 --> 00:10.0]
Just type rysh. You land in shell mode -- your familiar terminal, fully PTY-backed.

[00:10.0 --> 00:18.0]
In shell mode everything works like a normal terminal. Full color, full ANSI -- run any command you want.

[00:18.0 --> 00:26.0]
Double-press Escape to cycle the input mode. Watch the marker change to a less-than sign -- now you're talking to an AI agent.

[00:26.0 --> 00:40.0]
Ask anything. The agent sees your terminal context and answers right inside the pane, rendered as markdown.

[00:40.0 --> 00:46.0]
Escape again brings you back through the modes to shell. One pane, two ways to work.

[00:46.0 --> 00:53.0]
Ctrl+P enters pane mode. Press n to split right -- two independent panes, each its own shell and agent.

[00:53.0 --> 00:60.0]
Ctrl+T enters tab mode. Press n for a whole new tab. That's Rysh: every pane is a shell plus an AI agent.

